From: SenkOS
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: allwinner: rg35xx-2024: keep the DRAM voltage from SPL

H700 boards carry LPDDR4 (1.1 V) or LPDDR3 (1.2 V); SPL picks the type by
the boot0 DRAM straps and sets DCDC3 to match. A fixed 1.1 V in the dts
made the regulator core force 1.1 V at probe, under LPDDR3 too. With a
range it leaves the voltage SPL set.

Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/allwinner/sun50i-h700-anbernic-rg35xx-2024.dts
@@ -437,8 +437,9 @@
 
 			reg_dcdc3: dcdc3 {
 				regulator-always-on;
+				/* LPDDR4 or LPDDR3, set up by SPL; a range keeps its voltage */
 				regulator-min-microvolt = <1100000>;
-				regulator-max-microvolt = <1100000>;
+				regulator-max-microvolt = <1200000>;
 				regulator-name = "vdd-dram";
 			};
 
